WEBVTT

00:01.311 --> 00:03.191
I'm back.

00:03.271 --> 00:04.271
Subaru?

00:04.351 --> 00:05.731
Are you all right? Can you get up?

00:05.811 --> 00:07.061
Can you talk?

00:14.851 --> 00:15.771
Emilia.

00:15.851 --> 00:19.271
Emilia isn't the only one
who was worried about you!

00:21.601 --> 00:23.521
What's that look about, I suppose?

00:23.601 --> 00:27.101
It's as if you can't believe the
adorable Betty is standing before y—

00:27.191 --> 00:30.441
Beatrice! Beatrice! Beatrice!

00:30.521 --> 00:32.061
Wh-Wh-What?!

00:32.151 --> 00:34.441
This is too sudden, I suppose!

00:34.521 --> 00:36.731
You... You...

00:37.401 --> 00:39.601
Your face makes me feel so at ease!

00:39.691 --> 00:41.691
It's so cute that
I feel like I'm back home!

00:41.771 --> 00:43.191
I could fall in love!

00:43.271 --> 00:46.351
I really don't want to believe
you meant that as a compliment!

00:46.441 --> 00:49.811
Come on, Subaru. Don't start messing
with us the moment you wake up.

00:49.901 --> 00:53.401
We still don't even know
why you passed out...

00:55.481 --> 00:56.441
Subaru?

01:03.731 --> 01:05.311
What's wrong, I suppose?

01:05.401 --> 01:08.521
It's all right. Betty is here.

01:12.561 --> 01:14.311
Don't cry, Subaru.

01:14.901 --> 01:17.231
Just take slow, deep breaths.

01:17.731 --> 01:18.771
Calm down.

01:19.311 --> 01:23.941
Beatrice and I are both
right here with you.

03:04.481 --> 03:05.851
So, yeah...

03:05.941 --> 03:08.771
It seems like I lost my
memories in the archive.

03:08.851 --> 03:11.561
This might cause a lot
of trouble for you guys,

03:11.651 --> 03:14.351
but I'd appreciate your understanding.

03:14.441 --> 03:17.771
I'm sure you're all very
worried about Subaru.

03:18.271 --> 03:21.191
But we all need
to keep ourselves together,

03:21.271 --> 03:24.061
because no one feels more
anxious than he does right now.

03:24.151 --> 03:25.561
It doesn't look that way to me.

03:26.151 --> 03:28.901
What I want to know is: what kind
of stupid act is this, Barusu?

03:28.981 --> 03:30.731
It's not an act.

03:30.811 --> 03:33.901
I'm being super serious about
telling you all the truth.

03:33.981 --> 03:36.441
My heart's about to
explode from the anxiety.

03:36.521 --> 03:38.271
Very slick.

03:38.351 --> 03:39.981
You speak in that flippant tone
and expect us to believe—

03:40.061 --> 03:44.061
Subaru has no reason to
tell such sick lies.

03:44.401 --> 03:46.771
You should know that, I suppose.

03:50.101 --> 03:55.651
Honestly, Big Brother, you're
just hopeless, aren't you?

03:56.811 --> 03:58.601
What's with that reaction?

03:59.101 --> 04:01.731
You look like you just saw a ghost.

04:01.811 --> 04:03.851
Talk about rude.

04:04.811 --> 04:05.731
Meili...

04:05.811 --> 04:09.731
Oh? So you remember my name, huh?

04:09.811 --> 04:13.151
So what <i>did</i> you forget, then?

04:13.231 --> 04:16.691
I lost what they call episodic memory.

04:16.771 --> 04:19.311
I remember the names of
most people and things,

04:19.401 --> 04:23.191
but my memories of experiences I've
been through with others are murky.

04:23.901 --> 04:27.311
Does that include, say,
what happened yesterday?

04:29.311 --> 04:30.231
Yeah.

04:30.311 --> 04:32.271
Yesterday, eh?

04:33.061 --> 04:36.061
Well... yes, I suppose so.

04:36.151 --> 04:38.101
Really, Master? Again?

04:38.481 --> 04:42.401
How many times are you gonna forget me?

04:42.481 --> 04:45.811
Frankly, it's still a bit
difficult to accept...

04:46.651 --> 04:51.521
but it's likely there's a trap in this
tower that left Natsuki in this state.

04:51.601 --> 04:53.691
I think we should come to terms with that.

04:53.771 --> 04:55.771
Yeah. The archive is the most suspicious,

04:55.851 --> 04:59.191
since that's where Emilia-chan
and Beatrice found me.

04:59.271 --> 05:02.271
It was a pretty shady
place to begin with, too.

05:02.351 --> 05:03.191
"Chan"...

05:04.231 --> 05:06.771
Anyway, sorry I scared you all like that.

05:07.311 --> 05:09.231
I'm sure we all need
time to process things,

05:09.311 --> 05:10.981
so let's take a break.

05:11.401 --> 05:15.231
I'll go with Ram to fetch
water in the meantime.

05:16.981 --> 05:18.401
Let's go, Ram.

05:18.481 --> 05:21.851
You look like you were just about
to ask me to go with you, anyway.

05:23.151 --> 05:24.481
So lewd.

05:26.651 --> 05:29.901
So what was the idea behind that
ridiculous farce back there?

05:30.191 --> 05:33.231
Ram, it's true that I lost my memory.

05:33.311 --> 05:36.351
It's not a lie, a grift, or an evil plot.

05:38.191 --> 05:39.771
My memory is gone.

05:39.851 --> 05:43.941
I don't remember anything but your
names and the relationships we had.

05:44.021 --> 05:44.981
Stop it.

05:45.061 --> 05:49.851
I know we came to this tower to
get back a bunch of stuff we lost,

05:49.941 --> 05:52.271
and that we're trying to
get through its exams.

05:52.351 --> 05:53.771
But that's all.

05:54.191 --> 05:56.271
- My motive is—
- Stop it, Barusu.

05:56.351 --> 05:58.601
- No more.
- And Rem, too... I—

05:58.691 --> 05:59.771
Barusu!

06:03.811 --> 06:05.481
What are you playing at?

06:05.561 --> 06:06.561
What are these...

06:06.651 --> 06:08.981
these ridiculous lies?!

06:10.101 --> 06:12.101
They're not lies.

06:12.601 --> 06:14.731
So you're telling me to believe you?

06:15.231 --> 06:17.811
To believe something as stupid as...

06:17.901 --> 06:21.151
as you forgetting Rem?!

06:23.231 --> 06:25.481
I'm going to get Rem back.

06:27.401 --> 06:28.901
Who do you think you are?

06:28.981 --> 06:32.151
Get her back? You don't
even remember her, do you?!

06:32.231 --> 06:34.851
Barusu... You forgot Rem!

06:35.231 --> 06:36.691
I'll still get her back!

06:36.981 --> 06:39.901
Rem, and my memories, too! All of it!

06:40.271 --> 06:41.981
I'll do every damn thing there is to do,

06:42.101 --> 06:43.691
and then we'll all go home!

06:45.231 --> 06:48.981
We deserve that much, at least.

06:49.101 --> 06:51.691
Considering everything we've
been through in this tower...

06:52.061 --> 06:53.061
Barusu?

06:56.521 --> 06:59.851
Ram, I'm going to get Rem
and my memories back.

07:00.561 --> 07:02.561
I need you to help me do that.

07:04.351 --> 07:06.481
I need help from all of you!

07:06.561 --> 07:10.101
I get that you might never
forgive me for forgetting Rem.

07:10.191 --> 07:11.851
But I promise you this.

07:12.441 --> 07:13.401
What?

07:14.231 --> 07:15.771
I will see this through.

07:15.851 --> 07:19.601
If I give up, you can do
whatever you want to me.

07:20.101 --> 07:23.601
It'll be my penance for being
careless enough to lose my memories

07:23.691 --> 07:26.691
and making you cry.

07:37.521 --> 07:39.521
I'm not crying. Don't be stupid.

07:39.901 --> 07:44.601
C-Come on! It took a lot of
courage for me to say all that!

07:44.691 --> 07:46.151
What part of that took courage?

07:46.231 --> 07:48.191
You were just getting
yourself all worked up.

07:48.271 --> 07:50.981
Also, a promise from <i>you</i>?
Don't make me laugh.

07:51.101 --> 07:53.981
How many promises did I
break up until yesterday?!

07:54.101 --> 07:55.691
How many have you kept?

07:55.771 --> 07:57.601
That's easier to count?!

07:58.901 --> 08:02.901
Man, this Subaru Natsuki
really is worthless, huh?

08:02.981 --> 08:05.651
Why'd you even bring me to this tower?

08:05.731 --> 08:07.191
You butted in.

08:07.271 --> 08:10.771
Also, you did have a knack
for running your mouth.

08:10.851 --> 08:12.981
You could be counted on
to handle odd jobs, too.

08:13.101 --> 08:14.561
What else?

08:14.651 --> 08:16.851
I have short legs, my memory's bad,

08:16.941 --> 08:19.351
I'm a picky eater, and I
don't know when to give up.

08:19.771 --> 08:22.601
You had short legs, your memory
was bad, you were a picky eater,

08:22.691 --> 08:24.191
and you didn't know when to give up.

08:24.271 --> 08:25.561
Yeah, of course.

08:26.021 --> 08:27.061
And...

08:28.731 --> 08:30.561
you cared about Rem.

08:33.941 --> 08:37.191
Barusu, you've truly forgotten Rem, right?

08:38.021 --> 08:38.851
Yeah.

08:39.231 --> 08:41.811
Barusu, you're truly going
to remember her, right?

08:41.901 --> 08:43.851
Yeah. I will.

08:43.941 --> 08:46.101
Not just Rem, but everything else, too.

08:49.441 --> 08:52.311
Very well. I'll overlook this.

08:52.401 --> 08:53.811
On your feet, Barusu.

09:02.771 --> 09:03.771
I was...

09:04.231 --> 09:07.771
Subaru Natsuki was definitely here, right?

09:09.021 --> 09:13.771
Silly. He's just temporarily
invisible at the moment.

09:14.311 --> 09:16.941
Like a flower buried under the cold snow,

09:17.021 --> 09:20.021
he'll show himself once the
snowy season has passed.

09:22.441 --> 09:25.651
I'm sure that's all there is to it.

09:42.311 --> 09:43.851
Last time...

09:44.401 --> 09:46.191
and the time before that...

09:46.271 --> 09:48.521
this place was a complete mess.

09:50.351 --> 09:53.601
It'll happen again and soon.

09:54.101 --> 09:56.601
I have to stop it.

10:00.651 --> 10:01.481
So...

10:02.441 --> 10:03.771
for starters...

10:06.901 --> 10:07.731
Huh?!

10:08.101 --> 10:10.811
Wait! Wait! Wait! Wait! Wait!

10:17.351 --> 10:18.521
Whoa, there!

10:19.311 --> 10:21.401
Don't go taking that fall in my place.

10:22.061 --> 10:24.691
Now, let's talk.

10:24.771 --> 10:28.561
I'm gonna need you to take
responsibility for killing me.

10:31.271 --> 10:33.601
Responsibility for killing you?

10:33.691 --> 10:36.481
You're being weird again, Big Brother.

10:36.851 --> 10:40.651
After all, if I really wanted to kill you,

10:40.731 --> 10:43.651
wouldn't it have been much
easier to do it outside?

10:43.731 --> 10:47.101
Yeah, I'm sure you had
plenty of opportunities,

10:47.191 --> 10:49.061
but you didn't do it.

10:49.151 --> 10:50.771
Right? So—

10:50.851 --> 10:56.981
If your intent to kill me didn't exist
until this morning, that's different.

10:57.561 --> 11:02.271
Or should I say sometime after the whole
chain reaction that started last night?

11:03.061 --> 11:04.021
Don't tell me...

11:04.351 --> 11:09.271
Were you lying about losing your
memories just to set me up?

11:09.351 --> 11:11.271
Don't get the wrong idea, Meili.

11:11.601 --> 11:14.151
It's no lie that I lost my memory.

11:14.231 --> 11:15.901
It's true, which is why this is serious.

11:15.981 --> 11:20.401
That in itself brings up
some questions, but...

11:20.981 --> 11:24.061
How are you planning to
finish me off, then?

11:24.151 --> 11:26.811
Are you gonna push me off
these stairs for revenge?

11:26.901 --> 11:29.401
My mean little beasties
aren't with me now, so...

11:29.481 --> 11:32.941
I have no intention of
killing or hurting you.

11:33.771 --> 11:37.151
I intend to treat you the same
as I have been for all this time.

11:37.901 --> 11:41.731
Thankfully, I stopped your crime
before you could carry it out,

11:41.811 --> 11:45.651
so as long as I don't tell anyone,
we can pretend it never happened.

11:46.061 --> 11:47.311
Wh-What are you...

11:47.401 --> 11:50.851
But now you understand, right?

11:50.941 --> 11:53.981
It's gonna be pretty risky
to try to do anything to me.

11:54.101 --> 11:56.851
If you still want to try, well...

11:56.941 --> 11:58.521
let's at least talk it over.

11:59.021 --> 12:02.401
If something's bothering you,
I'll listen as best I can.

12:03.731 --> 12:04.901
Bothering me?

12:05.601 --> 12:06.981
Bothering me?

12:07.101 --> 12:10.271
If anything bothers me,
it's this situation right now!

12:10.351 --> 12:11.981
I can't believe you!

12:12.061 --> 12:16.351
You don't even know
what I was trying to do!

12:16.441 --> 12:18.691
This makes no sense otherwise!

12:19.401 --> 12:21.561
Because if you did...

12:21.651 --> 12:24.981
It was an unpredictable act on your part.

12:25.101 --> 12:26.981
Just an impulse.

12:27.101 --> 12:31.771
You just don't have any other
way of resolving problems.

12:32.101 --> 12:34.231
And that's not your fault.

12:35.401 --> 12:38.481
Because... murder is a habit.

12:39.441 --> 12:41.731
Don't talk like you know anything!

12:42.271 --> 12:45.061
What... What the hell...

12:45.151 --> 12:47.941
could you possibly know about me?!

12:48.021 --> 12:49.351
I do know.

12:50.151 --> 12:53.561
Meili, I know all about you.

12:53.651 --> 12:55.441
This might sound creepy,

12:55.521 --> 13:01.561
but I doubt there's anyone in this
world who knows you better than I do.

13:03.191 --> 13:04.521
Elsa Granhiert.

13:05.981 --> 13:09.691
She's the reason you tried
to kill me, right?

13:13.601 --> 13:16.521
I won't... let anyone...

13:21.191 --> 13:23.271
talk as if they understand me.

13:28.561 --> 13:33.151
<i>I think Elsa Granhiert was</i>
<i>an unbelievable woman.</i>

13:37.851 --> 13:39.941
I've been told to bring you back.

13:40.481 --> 13:42.691
So you'll be coming with me.

13:55.851 --> 13:56.771
What's wrong?

13:57.231 --> 13:59.271
Stop that. It tickles.

14:03.941 --> 14:07.851
I'm not too particular
about clothing, either,

14:07.941 --> 14:10.191
but you are definitely a strange one.

14:12.311 --> 14:13.981
So very temperamental.

14:14.561 --> 14:17.941
Aren't you, Meili?
It seems that's your name.

14:18.851 --> 14:21.061
It's stitched into those
rags you were wearing.

14:21.151 --> 14:23.271
They might belong to someone else,

14:23.351 --> 14:25.151
but not having a name to
call you is inconvenient, so...

14:26.601 --> 14:28.101
You are Meili.

14:28.651 --> 14:31.061
That's what I'm going to call you.

14:31.651 --> 14:36.151
If you say you lost everything,
forgot everything,

14:36.231 --> 14:40.521
then why don't I teach you?

14:41.311 --> 14:47.151
That's a mother's job, after all.

14:49.811 --> 14:54.351
<i>I think Elsa Granhiert</i>
<i>was a detestable woman.</i>

14:55.851 --> 14:57.481
Are you shivering?

14:58.351 --> 15:00.021
Perhaps you're cold?

15:06.191 --> 15:08.651
Stop that. It tickles.

15:09.231 --> 15:10.561
<i>I saw every job through.</i>

15:11.651 --> 15:13.851
<i>I modeled my methods after Elsa's.</i>

15:14.811 --> 15:16.731
<i>I learned to speak.</i>

15:16.811 --> 15:19.521
<i>I modeled my speech after Elsa's.</i>

15:20.271 --> 15:22.441
<i>I even wore clothes.</i>

15:22.521 --> 15:25.771
<i>I modeled my fashion sense after Elsa's.</i>

15:26.521 --> 15:30.771
<i>And I kept all that secret from Elsa.</i>

15:32.351 --> 15:36.191
<i>I think Elsa Granhiert</i>
<i>was a dreadful woman.</i>

15:36.481 --> 15:40.151
Meili, could you braid my
hair? I can't be bothered.

15:42.061 --> 15:43.981
Meili, are you listening?

15:44.061 --> 15:46.441
I asked you to braid my hair.

15:46.521 --> 15:48.561
Yes, I heard you.

15:48.651 --> 15:50.901
Honestly, you're such a slob.

16:00.521 --> 16:01.521
Grr.

16:01.601 --> 16:04.231
Excuse me? That tickles.

16:04.771 --> 16:05.901
Grr.

16:06.731 --> 16:08.191
You're such a funny girl.

16:11.521 --> 16:16.101
<i>I didn't want her to disappear after</i>
<i>she'd become a huge presence in my mind.</i>

16:16.651 --> 16:23.311
<i>She had become an unbelievable,</i>
<i>detestable, dreadful part of my life.</i>

16:24.021 --> 16:25.811
<i>Not even just "a part."</i>

16:25.901 --> 16:28.271
<i>She was so much bigger than that.</i>

16:29.401 --> 16:32.481
<i>So if that all had to be exposed...</i>

16:32.561 --> 16:34.231
<i>If it had to be trampled on...</i>

16:34.941 --> 16:38.231
<i>If Elsa Granhiert had to be killed...</i>

16:39.651 --> 16:41.561
<i>then Meili Portroute...</i>

16:46.401 --> 16:50.901
It would've been so much better
if you had just let me end it.

16:50.981 --> 16:52.901
Yeah, sorry.

16:52.981 --> 16:56.271
But while most people take off their
shoes when entering someone's home,

16:56.351 --> 17:01.401
it's the Natsuki family way to just
barge right into the hearts of others.

17:03.561 --> 17:05.851
You wanted to avenge her?

17:06.851 --> 17:08.441
I don't know.

17:08.521 --> 17:11.981
Even if that's the case, Elsa...

17:12.061 --> 17:13.981
...wouldn't have wanted that.

17:14.691 --> 17:16.601
I know that much.

17:19.101 --> 17:22.521
Why do you keep trying to help me?

17:22.851 --> 17:24.651
I've already forgotten almost everything.

17:24.731 --> 17:28.981
If I lost you, too, that'd be
one more thing for me to miss.

17:29.061 --> 17:30.271
I guess that's why.

17:31.401 --> 17:35.811
Meili, I get that you don't know
what to do with your own feelings.

17:35.901 --> 17:40.561
But I doubt you're gonna be able
to find all the answers right away.

17:40.651 --> 17:42.731
So let me handle things here.

17:43.311 --> 17:44.901
I won't let things go bad.

17:44.981 --> 17:48.691
Or at least, I'll do my best
not to let them go bad.

17:49.061 --> 17:52.101
As long as that's what you want, too.

17:52.651 --> 17:54.651
I can't... believe that.

17:55.401 --> 17:58.651
It's easy for you to
say whatever you want.

17:58.731 --> 18:00.981
Then don't consider it a promise with me.

18:01.101 --> 18:03.851
Consider it a promise with all of us.

18:04.811 --> 18:06.771
Yes. It's all right.

18:07.651 --> 18:11.021
I was listening, so I'm a
witness to that promise.

18:14.191 --> 18:16.441
You're a lifesaver, Emilia-chan!

18:16.521 --> 18:18.811
Frankly, I didn't even feel
like I was alive.

18:18.901 --> 18:20.691
That's what I should be saying!

18:20.771 --> 18:22.351
I can't believe you tried
to jump with her!

18:22.441 --> 18:25.691
I thought my heart was going
to leap out of my chest!

18:25.771 --> 18:26.811
Big Sister...

18:27.351 --> 18:29.441
You were... listening?

18:29.521 --> 18:34.481
Yes. Subaru said he wanted me
to help if you got into trouble.

18:37.481 --> 18:39.441
Listen, Meili.

18:39.521 --> 18:42.771
I believe what Subaru said.

18:42.851 --> 18:45.401
So I want you to believe him, too.

18:45.481 --> 18:46.901
Believe us both.

18:47.851 --> 18:53.481
This tower in the sand is too small a
place for you to make any big decisions.

18:53.561 --> 18:57.561
Look for your answers once we're
out of here and in a bigger place.

18:57.651 --> 19:00.691
We'll all do our very best, too.

19:03.601 --> 19:07.601
I don't want to forget about Elsa.

19:08.271 --> 19:09.851
Yeah. That's fine.

19:09.941 --> 19:12.941
There's no need to
forget someone you like.

19:13.021 --> 19:18.351
Though... it might be better if you
didn't try to do things the way she did.

19:22.271 --> 19:24.401
I see. It appears you took care of things.

19:24.851 --> 19:27.441
Not a bad job. My compliments.

19:27.521 --> 19:29.771
Perhaps I don't need to say it,

19:29.851 --> 19:33.941
but she has been waiting most
anxiously for your return.

19:34.021 --> 19:36.351
You're right. You didn't need to say that.

19:36.441 --> 19:38.061
Learn some restraint, Echidna.

19:38.151 --> 19:42.811
This is the attitude you take the moment
you find out I'm controlling this body.

19:42.901 --> 19:44.271
Just how I want it.

19:44.351 --> 19:46.771
Frankly, I was beside myself with worry.

19:47.101 --> 19:50.231
I held it in because Subaru
asked me to, I suppose.

19:52.651 --> 19:55.651
But are you really
sure about this, Master?

19:55.731 --> 19:58.351
She tried to kill you, y'know.

19:58.441 --> 20:01.021
You really don't think
she should be punished?

20:02.311 --> 20:06.401
It's fine. Meili's already
been through her punishment.

20:06.481 --> 20:10.271
Things turned out this
way because no one ever

20:10.351 --> 20:13.941
taught her why she was being punished.

20:14.021 --> 20:16.151
So I'm gonna teach her that going forward.

20:16.231 --> 20:18.441
I'll need your help, too, of course.

20:18.521 --> 20:19.481
Mine?

20:19.561 --> 20:23.231
Well, sure. Everyone in this
tower is gonna be her textbook.

20:23.311 --> 20:26.691
So don't do anything that
would set a bad example.

20:26.771 --> 20:29.651
Me, too?

20:29.731 --> 20:32.101
Master and me...

20:33.811 --> 20:35.401
Uh, what's with you?

20:35.481 --> 20:36.731
Nothing!

20:36.811 --> 20:39.651
I'll raise her up into a model
citizen! Just you watch!

20:39.731 --> 20:41.061
Hey, Big Brother!

20:41.151 --> 20:44.311
You put weird ideas in the naked
lady's head again, didn't you?!

20:44.401 --> 20:48.061
So I can take this to mean
that she is not an issue?

20:48.151 --> 20:49.521
Yep, that's right.

20:49.601 --> 20:52.351
Although what happens from
now on is up to Meili,

20:52.441 --> 20:55.061
who's gonna grow up watching our backs.

20:55.481 --> 20:58.271
So don't let your back
look spineless, yeah?

20:59.151 --> 21:02.311
I see. It's a matter of appearances.

21:02.401 --> 21:03.901
In that case, you can count on me.

21:03.981 --> 21:06.231
I expect the best, Mr. Knight!

21:06.601 --> 21:09.981
You and I are the closest things
she has to a father, after all.

21:11.851 --> 21:14.901
Then we will have to
give it our best effort.

21:14.981 --> 21:16.351
Yeah! Bring it on!

21:16.441 --> 21:19.521
Th-That's right! I'm going
to treat Meili as...

21:21.561 --> 21:25.351
FROM NOW ON

21:26.981 --> 21:28.311
Just a suggestion...

21:28.731 --> 21:31.191
but why don't we put my
amnesia aside for now?

21:31.271 --> 21:32.231
What?

21:32.691 --> 21:36.351
I'm really happy that you want
to help me get my memory back,

21:36.441 --> 21:40.521
but no one here believes the tower
had nothing to do with it, right?

21:41.231 --> 21:45.521
I'm saying there's some connection
between this tower and my amnesia.

21:46.481 --> 21:50.651
In other words, if we meet the
requirements to conquer the tower,

21:50.731 --> 21:53.851
we'll find the reason for
your amnesia in the process,

21:53.941 --> 21:55.981
and maybe even the key to fixing it.

21:56.271 --> 21:57.311
Is that it?

21:57.401 --> 21:59.521
Yes, yes! Exactly!

22:00.441 --> 22:01.441
Of course...

22:02.021 --> 22:05.521
that doesn't mean I think
I should just stay this way.

22:05.601 --> 22:08.271
But I want to do what we came here to do.

22:09.771 --> 22:13.401
I'll endure the difficulty
this time... but...

22:14.021 --> 22:15.021
But?

22:16.601 --> 22:21.811
Let me worry about you more than anyone
else every now and then, all right?

22:21.901 --> 22:23.811
Uh... sorry.

22:24.901 --> 22:27.561
Emilia said what I was
going to say, I suppose.

22:27.651 --> 22:29.271
You'd better reflect long
and hard on this.

22:29.351 --> 22:31.061
Yeah, I know.

22:31.151 --> 22:33.561
And what, specifically,
are we going to do?

22:33.851 --> 22:37.311
First of all, we need
to get past the exams.

22:37.401 --> 22:43.061
And the best way to do that is to figure
out what Reid's weakness is, right?

22:43.521 --> 22:44.521
So...

22:45.481 --> 22:49.941
why don't we all search the
archive for Reid's book?
